# Generated, environment-specific artifacts - reproducible via the pipeline.
# data/synthetic.csv is kept as a checked-in reference artifact (the README
# points to it directly). models/*.json (xgboost_model.json,
# feature_list.json) are also kept checked-in - monitor.py loads them at
# startup and a git-based deploy needs them present.
data/from_db.csv
# Regenerated by database/rebuild_historical.py (deterministic, seed=42) -
# 7.5MB, too large to be worth keeping in git history; unlike synthetic.csv
# this one isn't hand-referenced anywhere, so regenerating it is painless.
data/historical.csv
.claude/

# ml/train.py and ml/score.py's own output directory - both recreate it
# (os.makedirs(..., exist_ok=True)) on every run, so there's nothing here
# worth keeping in git history; defense/build_results_report.py expects
# outputs/model_comparison.csv to exist locally (run ml/train.py first).
outputs/
